1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
2: """lca_isaphys_probe.py -- the rung-3 WITNESS for `lcaisaphys' (#540).  A WITNESS, not a detector:
3: every row asserts the CORRECT behaviour, so it is RED on the committed build and GREEN after the fix.
4: 
5: THE DEFECT.  DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa) in src/devices/dev_lca.c forwards each sparse-window access to the
6: real ISA device with a NESTED `cpu->memory_rw(cpu, cpu->mem, LCA_ISA_BASE + port, ...)', on both arms,
7: with misc flags CACHE_NONE -- no PHYSICAL.  So the 33-bit PHYSICAL address 0x1d00003fd is handed to the
8: Alpha translator as a VIRTUAL one.  While ptbr == 0 the translator's identity hack (memory_alpha.c,
9: `if (!userMode && base == 0)') maps it straight through -- which is why no probe in this tree, all of
10: which run with ptbr == 0, has ever seen it.  Once a guest arms a page table, the inner address WALKS
11: the guest's tables and misses: a read answers a FALSE ZERO with success (the failed inner read leaves a
12: zeroed byte, and the read arm packs it and returns 1), a write is silently ABANDONED (#215), and every
13: miss prints `[ alpha_translate_v2p: 0x00000001d00003fd wasn't found ]'.
14: 
15: THE VEHICLE.  One unmodified `-E alpha -e alphabook1' process.  Controls first while ptbr == 0, then
16: CALL_PAL 0x30 (swpctx) with a PCB whose ptbr names an all-ZERO L1 page (PFN 0x828 -- NOT 0: ptbr 0 IS
17: the identity path, i.e. today's behaviour; and NOT the spec's 0x20a0, see ZERO_PFN), then the defect
18: accesses.  Every OUTER access is K0SEG,
19: which the translator identity-maps before any walk: a raw sparse VA would walk the window itself and
20: never enter the handler (the spec's trap 1).  The defect is the INNER forward, at 0x1d00003fd (read)
21: and 0x1d00003ff (write).
22: 
23:     WANTED ON THE COMMITTED BUILD: 9/13 -- rows 1-8 and 13 green, rows 9-12 RED.
24:     AFTER `CACHE_NONE | PHYSICAL' ON BOTH NESTED CALLS: 13/13, the same script.
25: 
26:     MEASURED ON THE COMMITTED BUILD, 2026-09-18: 9/13, no retry, the four defect rows exactly
27:     (artifacts/lcaisaphys/witness_HEAD_20260918/probe_HEAD.raw; build/ == HEAD on every file of the path).
28:     *** The spec predicted "8/13 (rows 1-8 and 13 green)" -- the ROWS were right and the TALLY was not:
29:     rows 1-8 plus row 13 is nine.  Its second arithmetic slip after the PFN (see ZERO_PFN). ***
30: 
31:     If any ARMING CONTROL (rows 2-7) is red, the vehicle was never armed.  The probe then prints
32:     LCAISAPHYS_CONTROL=DEAD and LCAISAPHYS_RESULT=0/0 and scores NOTHING (spec amendment 8): a failed
33:     swpctx leaves identity mapping on, which greens the defect rows on the committed build and would
34:     read as "no defect" -- a wrong-reason result presented as a measurement.
35: 
36: SPEC.  regress/artifacts/lcaisaphys/WITNESSSPEC_grok_20260917.txt (the rows, constants and traps) and
37: amendment 8 in regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/SPEC_AMENDMENTS_READ_BEFORE_BUILDING.md.  ONE DEPARTURE,
38: for a trap the spec does not name: the parent probe's pointer block lives at SCRATCH, a RAW 32-bit
39: address, which resolves only under identity mapping.  After swpctx every raw-VA load walks and misses,
40: so a pointer loaded through SCRATCH after the arm would never arrive and the defect accesses would
41: never run.  T0 is therefore re-based to k0(SCRATCH) by one LDQ BEFORE swpctx, and every later pointer
42: load goes through K0SEG.
43: 
44: ENCODER, session(), printed(), k0/SP/FLAT, SENT and load_const are copied from lca_isalane_probe.py;
45: CALL_PAL, the PCB layout and the "plant everything while ptbr is still 0" order from
46: alpha_pfnoffset_probe.py.  Neither file is imported.
47: 
48: Usage:  lca_isaphys_probe.py <gxemul-binary> [label]      (set LCAISAPHYS_RAW=<path> to keep the transcript)
49: """
50: import os, pty, re, select, sys, time
51: 
52: BIN   = sys.argv[1]
53: LABEL = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else "?"
54: MACH  = "alphabook1"
55: DUMMY = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "alpha_dummy.bin")
56: if not os.path.exists(DUMMY):                 # as alpha_pfnoffset_probe.py: an 8-byte dummy kernel
57:     with open(DUMMY, "wb") as f:
58:         f.write(b"\0" * 8)
59: 
60: # ---------------------------------------------------------------- encoder (memory format only)
61: ZERO, T0, T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, T6, T7 = 31, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8
62: A0 = 16                                       # a0: the PCB address for swpctx
63: V  = 22                                       # t8: holds store VALUES only and is never printed, so
64:                                               # the six printed destinations t2..t7 stay unique
65: 
66: def mem(op, ra, rb, disp):
67:     assert -32768 <= disp <= 32767, "displacement %d out of range" % disp
68:     return (op << 26) | (ra << 21) | (rb << 16) | (disp & 0xffff)
69: 
70: def LDA (ra, disp, rb=ZERO): return mem(0x08, ra, rb, disp)
71: def LDAH(ra, disp, rb=ZERO): return mem(0x09, ra, rb, disp)
72: def LDBU(ra, disp, rb):      return mem(0x0a, ra, rb, disp)   # BWX byte load  -> memory_rw len 1
73: def LDQ (ra, disp, rb):      return mem(0x29, ra, rb, disp)   # quadword load  -> memory_rw len 8
74: def STB (ra, disp, rb):      return mem(0x0e, ra, rb, disp)   # BWX byte store -> memory_rw len 1
75: def CALL_PAL(n):             return n & 0x3ffffff
76: 
77: def load_const(reg, val):                     # 32-bit only, exactly as the parent
78:     lo = val & 0xffff
79:     hi = (val >> 16) & 0xffff
80:     if lo >= 0x8000:
81:         hi = (hi + 1) & 0xffff
82:     ops = [LDAH(reg, hi if hi < 0x8000 else hi - 0x10000)]
83:     if lo:
84:         ops.append(LDA(reg, lo if lo < 0x8000 else lo - 0x10000, reg))
85:     return ops
86: 
87: SENT = 0x0bad1d8a                             # the parent's pre-seed: a load that does not complete
88: def sent(reg): return load_const(reg, SENT)   # leaves it; low byte 0x8a has bits 5-6 CLEAR, so it
89:                                               # cannot fake LSR_FIXED under the 0x60 mask
90: 

